<p class="lab-step">{{ site.lab_slides.strategic_tradeoffs.label }}</p>
<h2 class="dilemma__title">{{ site.lab_slides.strategic_tradeoffs.title }}</h2>
<p class="business-intro">{{ site.lab_slides.strategic_tradeoffs.intro }}</p>
<section class="strategy-lab" aria-label="Interactive weighted strategy comparison">
<fieldset class="strategy-presets"><legend>What should our company prioritize?</legend>
<label><input type="radio" name="strategy-priority" value="acquisition" checked> Integrate acquisitions faster</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="strategy-priority" value="scientific"> Differentiate scientific workflows</label>
<label><input type="radio" name="strategy-priority" value="cost"> Control long-term costs</label>
</fieldset>
<div class="strategy-scores" aria-live="polite">
<div class="strategy-score" data-strategy-option="glean"><div class="strategy-score__head"><strong>Glean · buy</strong><span data-strategy-score="glean">3.20 / 5</span></div><div class="strategy-score__track"><div class="strategy-score__bar" data-strategy-bar="glean" style="width:64%"></div></div></div>
<div class="strategy-score" data-strategy-option="hybrid"><div class="strategy-score__head"><strong>Hybrid · adapt</strong><span data-strategy-score="hybrid">3.15 / 5</span></div><div class="strategy-score__track"><div class="strategy-score__bar" data-strategy-bar="hybrid" style="width:63%"></div></div></div>
<div class="strategy-score" data-strategy-option="custom"><div class="strategy-score__head"><strong>Own build</strong><span data-strategy-score="custom">2.55 / 5</span></div><div class="strategy-score__track"><div class="strategy-score__bar" data-strategy-bar="custom" style="width:51%"></div></div></div>
</div>
<div class="strategy-insight"><strong>My interpretation</strong><p data-strategy-insight>Glean narrowly leads; the 0.05-point gap over hybrid is not a basis for a binding supplier decision. Validate both routes through a focused test.</p></div>
<details class="lab-more"><summary>See criteria, weights and calculation</summary>
<div class="strategy-table-scroll"><table class="strategy-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision criterion</th><th>Glean</th><th>Hybrid</th><th>Build</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Acquisition integration <span data-strategy-weight="0">30%</span></th><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td></tr>
<tr><th>Scientific fit <span data-strategy-weight="1">25%</span></th><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>4</td></tr>
<tr><th>3-year economics <span data-strategy-weight="2">20%</span></th><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><th>Data governance <span data-strategy-weight="3">15%</span></th><td>3</td><td>3</td><td>3</td></tr>
<tr><th>Exit flexibility <span data-strategy-weight="4">10%</span></th><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>3</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Weighted score = sum of criterion scores (1–5) multiplied by their weights. The assumptions are preliminary; governance, permission safety and permitted processing locations remain non-negotiable gates, not offsets in the score.</p>
</details>
<p class="scenario-note">This model tests strategic priorities, not product performance. Acquisition-specific source onboarding, scientific quality and complete supplier pricing must be verified before an investment decision.</p>
</section>